    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήπουθεν</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμ-θε</span></b>  before a consonant, <i><span class="en">
			Bato
			7.3
		</span></i>), indef. Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήπου</span>
			, chiefly used before a vowel (before a consonant, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ion</u>
				534a
			</span></i>, etc.), freq. in Com., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				296
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				140
			</span></i>, etc.; in answer to a rhetorical question, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ δ., ἀλλά . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					6.36
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				27.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				62e
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
